course: dictionary
lesson: 1872
title: Collaborate: working together, or helping the enemy
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To collaborate means to work together with other people to make something or reach a shared goal. Its parts are co, meaning together, and labour, meaning work. «We collaborated on the poster» means we made it as a team, with each person adding ideas and effort.
explain: The word also has a serious meaning in history. To collaborate can mean to help an enemy who has taken over your country, especially in a war. «Some people collaborated with the invaders» is a clue: invaders are enemies who take land by force, so this sense is about helping them.
explain: Use context to choose the right meaning. Look at the words around it: poster, project or team point to working together, while invaders, war or enemy point to the history meaning. Then swap in "worked together". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the friendly meaning.
fact: Collaborate is a verb: collaborate, collaborates, collaborated, collaborating.
fact: Common phrases are «collaborate with someone», «collaborate on a project» and «collaborate closely».
fact: In school, teachers ask you to collaborate in group work, science projects and team problem-solving.
fact: In history, «collaborated» can mean helping an enemy who has taken over your country, especially in a war.
fact: Yad Vashem, Israel's Holocaust memorial, has recognised over 2,600 Ukrainians as Righteous Among the Nations: non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews.
exercise: «We collaborated on the poster.» What does collaborated mean here? | *Worked together to make the poster | Argued and walked away from the poster | Hid the poster from the teacher | Tore up the poster
exercise: «Some people collaborated with the invaders.» In history, what does collaborated mean in this sentence? | *Helped the enemy who had taken over their country | Built a new school | Ran away from the war | Fought bravely against the invaders
exercise: Which word in this sentence means to work together? «The team will collaborate closely on the robot.» | will | robot | team | *collaborate
test: «The engineers collaborated to design the bridge.» What does collaborated mean? | *Worked together | Sold | Quarrelled | Hid from
test: Mr Patel asks the class to collaborate in pairs. What does he want them to do? | Go outside to play | Leave early | *Work together in pairs | Work alone and quietly
exam: Read this: «Some other people collaborated (helped the Nazis) and most were too afraid to act.» Why is collaborated a bad word in this sentence? | Because it means being late for school | Because it means going to sleep | Because it means painting pictures | *Because it means helping an enemy who has taken over, which is a betrayal
